SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Charalambos\, patron of Paxos\, Gaios
LOCATION:Gaios\, Paxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Charalambos is the protector of Paxos and his 10 February feast is the island's winter high point: hierarchical liturgy at his church in Gaios with the Metropolitan of Corfu\, the mayor and the schools\, then a procession of the icon along the waterfront and a reception. Boats from Corfu run all winter\; almost nothing else is open\, which is the point.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paxos/#gaios-feast-of-agios-charalambos-patron-of-paxos-gaios
